        <tr>
          <td><span class="postbody"><img src="images/smiles/icon_eek.gif" alt="Shocked" border="0" />  hola folks~
<br />

<br />
Wenn and I tooled around with DAoC a while back, the new graphics are pretty nice but the game still seems to be lacking *something*.
<br />

<br />
EQ is having some problems, hard to say whats wrong but, seems like massive numbers of the "old timers" are bailing out lately. But on the other hand with the invent of LDoN, now there's a really nice feature for the casual gamer, no more "what do we do" syndrome just pick a camp, get a few friends ( you can do them with virtually any class combo ) and away you go on your own little personal dungeon crawl. It all takes little more than an hour a wack yet provides some meaningful advancment. Only problem I have is that they aren't really on par with elemental plane exp/loot verses time spent, not really a concern for most players though.
<br />

<br />
I know a few people that plan on playing Horizons, so I might, if nothing else, check it out. Most of the beta testers I know, don't really like it much, so I don't know what to expect out of it honestly.
<br />

<br />
Tron2.0 was really fun though  <img src="images/smiles/icon_biggrin.gif" alt="Very Happy" border="0" /><br />_________________<br />~Gundail~</span><span class="gensmall"><i></i></span></td>
